@page "/replay"
@inject ReplayLibrary Replays

<PageTitle>Recorded conversations — Prowlers &amp; Paragons</PageTitle>

<h1>Watch one being built</h1>

@* "a costed character back" rather than "a legal one": one of these is a Villain, who is
   over the tier's points and is meant to be, because Ch.9 gives a Villain no budget. The page
   that plays him declines to call him legal, so this one must not promise it. *@
<p class="muted">
    Conversations in which somebody described a character in ordinary words and got a costed,
    checked one back. They are recordings — each was said once, and is played back exactly as
    it was. The figures beside them are not recorded: every Hero Point cost and every finding
    is worked out on the page, from the character the recording carries, as you reveal it.
</p>

@if (Replays.Problem is not null)
{
    <Panel Title="The recordings did not load" NoPrint="true">
        <p class="small">
            Nothing else on this site is affected — you can build a character normally. What
            went wrong: @Replays.Problem
        </p>
    </Panel>
}

<div class="grid replay-list">
    @foreach (var conversation in Replays.Conversations)
    {
        <Panel Title="@conversation.Title" NoPrint="true">
            <Head>
                @if (conversation.Villain)
                {
                    <span class="tag warn">Villain</span>
                }
            </Head>
            <ChildContent>
                <p class="small muted">@conversation.Blurb</p>
                <NavLink class="btn primary" href="@($"replay/{conversation.Id}")">
                    Play it
                </NavLink>
            </ChildContent>
        </Panel>
    }
</div>

<Panel Title="Why these are recordings and not a conversation you can have" NoPrint="true">
    <p class="small">
        Holding the conversation live would mean this site paying for the model that answers
        you, and it is a site with nothing behind it — no accounts, no server, nothing that
        costs anything to run. So instead of a worse imitation of the real thing, these are
        the real thing, recorded.
    </p>
    <p class="small">
        You <em>can</em> have it live, if you already have Claude. The rules engine on this
        page also ships as a small program you connect to it, after which you describe a
        character to your own assistant and it asks the same two or three questions and builds
        the same character. The setup guide is in the project's repository, at docs/MCP-SETUP.md.
    </p>
</Panel>
